  "manual": {
    "notes": [
      "DEATH DATE CORRECTED (research 2026-07-03): tree's own record carries two conflicting unsourced death entries, 1704 and 1709; independent sources (WikiTree Woodbury-117, FamilySearch, Find A Grave #94057512, mccallroots.com) agree he died 5 Jul 1704 in Beverly, MA — the 1709 entry appears to be an error and should be disregarded. Those same sources give his birthplace as Salem, MA (not Gloucester as this tree has it) and document offices not in the tree: freeman (1668), selectman (1679), deacon (1689), and deputy to the Massachusetts General Court (1689); he married Sarah Dodge 2 Jul 1667. Family tradition (not primary-sourced) credits him with sheltering people accused during the Salem witch trials on his property."
    ]
  }
